cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this reproducibility package, please cite the archived
  release. If you refer to the method itself, please cite the
  accompanying article.
title: "DMS-SI-Mix: Reproducibility Package"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-01"
type: dataset
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21671272
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21671272
    description: Concept DOI, resolves to the latest version
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21671273
    description: Version DOI of release 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aguilarmadeira/DMS-SI-MIX"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for the two-space scale-invariant Direct
  Multisearch method DMS-SI-Mix. Version 1.1.0 contains the data,
  configurations, run logs, final archives, metric tables, and
  validation scripts supporting the reported experiments, including
  the MORAP-NM exact Pareto front with integrity hashes and the
  categorical-neighborhood ablation, together with the external
  mixed-variable NSGA-II reference point on MORAP-NM (nine
  configurations, 30 seeds each, with its harness, aggregation and
  integrity-audit scripts). It does NOT yet contain the MATLAB
  solver, which is added in version 2.0.0 on acceptance of the
  accompanying article.
authors:
  - family-names: Madeira
    given-names: J. F. A.
    email: aguilarmadeira@tecnico.ulisboa.pt
    affiliation: >-
      IDMEC-IST, Instituto Superior Tecnico, Universidade de Lisboa,
      Portugal; ISEL-IPL, Lisboa, Portugal
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9523-3808"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - derivative-free optimization
  - multiobjective optimization
  - direct multisearch
  - mixed-variable optimization
  - scale invariance
  - categorical variables
  - deterministic neighborhood rotation
  - reproducibility
